Fit dialogs and bubbles to a phone screen and to the shell's insets.

Absorbs, in this order: ohos-device-chooser-width.patch, ohos-dialog-width-fits-screen.patch, ohos-dialog-preferred-width.patch, ohos-bubble-anchor-top-center.patch, ohos-tab-modal-shell-insets.patch, ohos-browser-modal-shell-insets.patch. Their descriptions follow.

--- ohos-device-chooser-width.patch

Fit the device chooser inside a phone screen.

DeviceChooserContentView asks for a fixed 402dp of width. On the device this
port runs on the work area is 377dp, and a bubble is not shrunk to fit: the
chooser was laid out 462dp wide (measured, bounds=34,-4 462x483), its right
edge past the display, and the Connect button sat where no touch could reach
it. Selecting a device by touch worked and still could not be confirmed.

The width is now the smaller of 402dp and what the work area leaves once the
bubble frame is accounted for. Desktop is untouched.

--- ohos-dialog-width-fits-screen.patch

Stop a dialog being snapped wider than the screen it is shown on.

BubbleFrameView snaps any bubble that has buttons to one of Chrome's dialog
widths. The smallest of those is wider than this port's phone screen, so the
Bluetooth device chooser was laid out 462dp wide on a 376dp work area, its
right edge past the display and its Connect button somewhere no touch could
reach. Measured on device, with the chooser's own contents already clamped to
312dp: contents_preferred=312x320, work_area=0,0 376x809, bubble bounds
34,-4 462x483. The width was not coming from the contents.

Snapping is a nicety. Fitting on the screen is not, on a device where there is
nowhere else for the dialog to go. The snapped width is now capped at the work
area less a small margin, and min_width still wins over the cap -- a frame
narrower than its own contents is not a size, it is a broken layout, and the
contents-side clamp in ohos-device-chooser-width.patch is what keeps the two
from meeting there.

This is deliberately not limited to the chooser. Every dialog with buttons is
snapped by this function, and none of them fit either.

--- ohos-dialog-preferred-width.patch

Keep dialogs that ask for a preferred width on a phone screen.

ohos-dialog-width-fits-screen.patch capped GetSnappedDialogWidth, but dialogs
that take DISTANCE_MODAL_DIALOG_PREFERRED_WIDTH (or the large variant, or the
standalone bubble width) directly bypass it. The WebAuthn "use a phone or
tablet" QR sheet is one: it was laid out past the right edge of the screen and
cut off. On OHOS those metrics are capped to the work area as well.

--- ohos-bubble-anchor-top-center.patch

Put the anchorless bubbles across the top centre, not in the corner.

With no Views toolbar to anchor to, every branch of
GetPageInfoAnchorConfiguration falls through to an empty configuration whose
arrow is TOP_LEFT, and GetPageInfoAnchorRect returns a zero-size rect
kNoToolbarLeftOffset (40dp) in from the window's left edge. So the Bluetooth
chooser and the permission prompt both hung off the top-left corner of a phone
screen -- measured on device as anchor_rect=40,0 0x0.

The offset exists so that a bubble shown in fullscreen does not obscure the
fullscreen bubble, which is a trade this port does not have to make: its
browser UI is drawn in ArkTS, so nothing of Chrome's is up there to collide
with. The anchor becomes a zero-height rect across the top of the window and
the arrow becomes TOP_CENTER, which hangs the bubble from the top edge,
centred -- where a phone-shaped Chrome puts it. The rect sits below the
shell's top bar, which the shell reports to the bridge: from the window's own
top edge the bubble went under the status bar and the address bar, with only
its buttons showing (the local network access prompt on baidu.com).

This is the shared anchor for the page info bubble, the permission prompt and
the device chooser, so all three move together, which is the point.

--- ohos-tab-modal-shell-insets.patch

Keep tab-modal dialogs between the shell's top bar and dock.

A tab-modal dialog -- the extension and theme install confirmations, and the
other dialogs Chromium shows over a tab -- hangs from the bottom of the Views
toolbar. This port has no Views toolbar on screen: its browser UI is drawn in
ArkTS over the page, so the dialog went to the very top of the window, under
the status bar and the shell's address bar, with only its buttons showing and
taps on them taken by the address bar (measured on a Mate 70 Pro+ with an
extension install from www.crxsoso.com).

On OHOS TabModalDialogHost keeps the dialog's top at or below the shell's top
bar and its maximum height within the room above the dock and the gesture
bar, both as the shell reported them to the bridge. While a tab is blocked by
such a dialog, the bridge holds the top bar and dock shown, so that room is
the room there is; they go back to following the page when it closes.

--- ohos-browser-modal-shell-insets.patch

Keep browser-modal dialogs between the shell's top bar and dock.

ohos-tab-modal-shell-insets.patch moved tab-modal dialogs below the shell's
top bar, but a browser-modal dialog -- the extension install prompt for a
.crx the shell asks to install -- is placed by BrowserViewLayout's own
dialog host, below a Views toolbar this port does not show. On a Mate 70
Pro+ it still opened under the status bar and the address bar, its title
hidden.

On OHOS BrowserModalDialogHostViews keeps the dialog's top at or below the
shell's top bar and its maximum height within the room above the dock and
gesture bar, from the insets the shell reported for the window.

Generated for Chromium 154.0.8037.51 after chromium-154-harmonyos.patch.
Apply with:

  git -C /path/to/chromium/src apply /path/to/patches/ohos-phone-dialogs.patch

